    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0823" n="811" xml:id="pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62114 Sick/9–1044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Göteborg</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Corcoran</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Göteborg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-10">September 10,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received September 10—8:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. <hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> sailed at 8:30 this morning September
                    10 carrying 967 passengers of which 42 are Canadians, 689 British and 236
                    American.</p>
                <p>Total repatriates on three vessels<anchor n="52" xml:id="d739-f1"/> approximately
                        2700.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d739-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corcoran</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d739-f1" n="52" xml:id="d739-f1-content">
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm, Drottningholm</hi>, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arundel Castle</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d739-f2" n="53" xml:id="d739-f2-content">
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> arrived on September 26 at Jersey
                    City, N. J. For additional data concerning (1) the American and German nationals
                    exchanged, (2) repatriation of British personnel at the same time, at Göteborg,
                    and (3) detention of the exchange ship at Kristiansand, Norway, by German
                    authorities and the forcible removal from the vessel of two crew members, see
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, October 1, 1944, pp.
                    355–356.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
